SAFETY-NETTING ADVICE

The injection provided will help the pain. You must remain as still as possible. If you feel a sudden, extreme worsening of the pain or vomit any fresh blood, tell the paramedics immediately upon their arrival.

PATIENT EDUCATION

Treatment Explanation: Your long-standing liver cirrhosis has likely caused a new, rapidly growing mass to form within the liver tissue itself. This mass is causing the continuous pain and physically blocking the blood flow through your liver, which is why the fluid is suddenly building up so rapidly despite your medications. The hospital will perform a specialized scan to definitively identify the mass and will drain the fluid to relieve your severe discomfort.
Actionable Steps: Do not take any further diuretic tablets. The mass is physically blocking the fluid from leaving your abdomen, and continuing the tablets will only aggressively dehydrate your kidneys without reducing the swelling, leading to dangerous kidney failure.

